---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Our Own ASM Mining Operations"
  description="Ethical, sustainable artisanal and small-scale mining operations run by Orivia in Sub-Saharan Africa."
>
  <section class="section service-page">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow"><a href="/what-we-do">&larr; What We Do</a></p>
      <h1 class="reveal">01 &middot; Our Own ASM Mining Operations</h1>
      <p class="lede reveal">
        Our own operations are where our standards get tested first, before
        we ever advise someone else on theirs.
      </p>

      <div class="body-grid">
        <div class="reveal">
          <h2>Environmental stewardship</h2>
          <p>
            We employ methods designed to minimise ecological impact and
            regenerate mined landscapes: restoration, water protection and
            biodiversity preservation built into every project. We measure
            and report our footprint so it can actually be managed, site by
            site.
          </p>
          <h2>Community and women&rsquo;s participation</h2>
          <p>
            We work directly with local communities on shared growth:
            education, fair income and empowerment, with particular focus
            on women&rsquo;s participation in mining regions. Local leaders
            and families are involved at every step, building social
            systems that outlast any single project.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="reveal">
          <h2>Why we still operate</h2>
          <p>
            Every part of our advisory work, for ASM operators, large-scale
            miners, investors, buyers and traders, is grounded in the fact
            that we run a site ourselves. That keeps our recommendations
            realistic: we know what a given standard actually costs to
            reach, and how long it takes, because we&rsquo;ve reached it
            ourselves.
          </p>
          <h2>Frontier market context</h2>
          <p>
            Operating in Sub-Saharan Africa means building standards that
            hold up under conditions many international frameworks
            don&rsquo;t account for: infrastructure gaps, informal land
            tenure, and supply chains that run through several
            intermediaries before reaching a formal buyer.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="cta-row">
        <a class="pill-btn" href="/contact">Talk to us about our operations</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .service-page .eyebrow {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .lede {
    max-width: 720px;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    margin-bottom: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem);
  }

  .body-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: var(--gap);
    margin-bottom: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4rem);
  }

  .cta-row {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    padding-top: 2rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 800px) {
    .body-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
